<title>EGYPT: Egypt buys 15,000 T sunflower oil, cancels soyoil.</title>
<headline>Egypt buys 15,000 T sunflower oil, cancels soyoil.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Egyptian state's Holding Company for Food Industries said on Wednesday it bought 15,000 tonnes plus or minus five percent of crude sunflower seed oil at $533.25 per tonne from Atlantic of Argentina for delivery in the first half of April.</p>
<p>The company's head of the sales sector, Muharram Ghanem, told Reuters the firm cancelled a tender to buy between 5,000 and 10,000 tonnes of degummed soy oil.</p>
<p>--Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
